      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. Let me write an improved, more understandable version.\n\nThe test verifies two sequential `flatten` calls:\n1. With `stopAtNonOption=true`: a non-option token causes \"--\" to be prepended and null elements to be consumed, yielding 7 tokens\n2. With `stopAtNonOption=false` on that result: null tokens are silently skipped, leaving only the 2 non-null tokensNow I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully (`COMPILE_OK`). The refactored version preserves identical runtime behaviour while adding descriptive variable names (`parser`, `emptyOptions`, `argsWithNulls`, `flattenedWithStop`, `flattenedWithoutStop`), assertion messages that explain the expected counts, and a Javadoc comment that explains the two-phase flattening logic being exercised."
